<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bernhard, Duke of Saxony</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1140–1212</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Bernhard of Anhalt</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bernhard, a younger son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/albert-the-bear">Albert the Bear</a> of the Ascanian house, was Count of Anhalt and from 1180 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/duke-of-saxony">Duke of Saxony</a>. He received the ducal title after the fall of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-the-lion">Henry the Lion</a>, but only with the eastern remnants of the old duchy, while <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/westphalia">Westphalia</a> went to the Archbishop of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cologne">Cologne</a>. His descendants divided his lands into Anhalt, Saxe-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wittenberg">Wittenberg</a> and Saxe-Lauenburg.</p></div>
